    "body": "- [x] This PR does not suggest changes based on personal taste (enabling new or changing value of existing option, install new plugin)\r\n\r\nThis seems like something that would be pretty useful to folks trying this, especially since some of the mappings are a departure from the norm. \r\n\r\nIf it is really trying to be a starer config in the same token as kickstart, I think all beginners should have easy access to find keymappings.",
    "closed_at": "2025-10-16T12:51:22Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nAlthough I do understand the reasoning, I personally don't remember ever having good experience with this sort of pickers. Mapping descriptions are rarely enough for a meaningful query based search.\r\n\r\nIn my experience, the best long term solution to getting used to the mappings is:\r\n- Use 'mini.clue' clues for `<Leader>` based mappings (the main source of custom mappings).\r\n- Use `<Leader>ek` or `<Leader>em` to open and explore mappings in a buffer.\r\n\r\nI'd also like to keep `<Leader>fk` for potentially something else (not sure yet what).",
            "created_at": "2025-10-16T12:51:22Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/MiniMax/pull/11#issuecomment-3410753500",
            "id": 3410753500,
